1
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:34,150
The third floor of the dungeon.

2
00:01:34,950 --> 00:01:40,710
After you go through the graveyard in the tallest tower's forest, you'll arrive inside the golden castle.

3
00:01:41,690 --> 00:01:47,550
Once opulent, the interior is now covered in dust and mold, a shadow of its former glory.

4
00:01:48,550 --> 00:01:51,110
Deep within, footsteps echo through the halls.

5
00:01:51,410 --> 00:01:57,190
They could belong to another adventurer, or to a former resident, now undead.

6
00:01:57,190 --> 00:02:00,010
That there's a skeleton.

7
00:02:03,130 --> 00:02:04,150
That's a human.

8
00:02:07,810 --> 00:02:08,750
That's a ghoul.

9
00:02:08,810 --> 00:02:10,850
You're weirdly accurate, but how?

10
00:02:11,110 --> 00:02:14,810
The footsteps of people, skeletons, and zombies all sound totally different.

11
00:02:19,610 --> 00:02:23,010
We'll go left. There are golems down that other corridor.

12
00:02:23,010 --> 00:02:30,490
Golems. Magical creatures made from mud, dirt, and stone, and humanoid in shape.

13
00:02:30,990 --> 00:02:33,950
Puppets that follow their creators every order.

14
00:02:34,610 --> 00:02:34,990
Wait.

15
00:02:34,990 --> 00:02:39,110
Before you say it, we are not eating golems.

16
00:02:39,270 --> 00:02:40,910
They're 99% rocks and dirt.

17
00:02:41,110 --> 00:02:42,690
They're not alive. They're magical.

18
00:02:43,210 --> 00:02:44,850
Heck, even I can make one of them.

19
00:02:45,390 --> 00:02:46,270
Teach me how.

20
00:02:46,370 --> 00:02:46,730
No.

21
00:02:47,030 --> 00:02:49,750
If she taught you how, we all know what you'd do with it.

22
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:53,250
If there's golems down there, I need to get some things from them.

23
00:02:53,910 --> 00:02:54,530
Follow me.

24
00:02:54,530 --> 00:02:58,870
My base camp.

25
00:02:59,210 --> 00:03:01,350
It's not much, but make yourselves to home.

26
00:03:02,070 --> 00:03:02,550
Whoa.

27
00:03:03,890 --> 00:03:05,050
Do you live here?

28
00:03:05,510 --> 00:03:07,050
Nah, I don't sleep here much.

29
00:03:07,850 --> 00:03:10,390
I do my hunting on the second and fourth floors.

30
00:03:10,770 --> 00:03:15,810
Around about every month or so, I go to the village to get spice and other stuff I'm low on.

31
00:03:16,450 --> 00:03:19,770
In fact, I ran into you on my way back from a supply run.

32
00:03:20,790 --> 00:03:22,550
There's not much to eat here on the third.

33
00:03:23,010 --> 00:03:27,510
Most of the monsters you find are either rotting away or just bones walking around.

34
00:03:27,990 --> 00:03:30,470
But we got golems.

35
00:03:30,790 --> 00:03:32,810
Hoo boy, they are something special.

36
00:03:33,250 --> 00:03:37,750
Their bodies are filled with nutrients, and they maintain a consistent temperature and humidity.

37
00:03:38,230 --> 00:03:40,630
A useful critter if there ever was one.

38
00:03:41,770 --> 00:03:43,890
So what you're saying is...

39
00:03:43,890 --> 00:03:46,050
You use them as a walking veggie patch?

40
00:03:46,170 --> 00:03:47,450
That's an affront to farming!

41
00:03:47,930 --> 00:03:49,710
And to magic scoloring, too!

42
00:03:50,010 --> 00:03:50,990
What's the harm?

43
00:03:51,230 --> 00:03:54,930
I might not like magic much, but I dang well appreciate golems.

44
00:03:54,930 --> 00:03:57,810
They're a whole lot better than your average cropland.

45
00:03:58,370 --> 00:04:01,010
Bugs are never a problem, because they kill them all.

46
00:04:01,430 --> 00:04:03,450
They deal with vegetable thieves, too.

47
00:04:04,010 --> 00:04:05,730
Who'd steal veggies off a golem?

48
00:04:06,130 --> 00:04:09,150
They keep their water levels perfect so they don't dry out.

49
00:04:09,570 --> 00:04:12,370
And anything you plant on them is guaranteed to grow.

50
00:04:12,710 --> 00:04:14,230
They do all the hard work for you.

51
00:04:14,450 --> 00:04:17,650
But like any field of crops, they need tendon now and again.

52
00:04:18,150 --> 00:04:20,310
That's how come I set up my base camp here.

53
00:04:24,930 --> 00:04:37,630
No way!

54
00:04:38,470 --> 00:04:39,650
What are you gonna do?

55
00:04:39,770 --> 00:04:40,650
Should we help?

56
00:04:40,810 --> 00:04:41,070
Nope!

57
00:04:41,070 --> 00:05:01,350
That's amazing.

58
00:05:01,530 --> 00:05:02,810
He knows how to handle them.

59
00:05:03,310 --> 00:05:06,590
How does he know where the magic cores are to disable them?

60
00:05:07,150 --> 00:05:08,670
I think I know how.

61
00:05:08,670 --> 00:05:10,070
All done.

62
00:05:11,010 --> 00:05:13,390
You mind helping me harvest all the veggies off them?

63
00:05:14,130 --> 00:05:16,950
I couldn't even tell these were gardens on their backs at first.

64
00:05:17,370 --> 00:05:21,510
Since the plants live on the golems, are they, like, parasites to them?

65
00:05:22,150 --> 00:05:22,630
Nope.

66
00:05:22,710 --> 00:05:24,310
It's a symbiotic kind of thing.

67
00:05:24,570 --> 00:05:28,990
Once the plants take root, they hold the dirt together and make the golem's body stronger.

68
00:05:29,710 --> 00:05:30,150
Really?

69
00:05:30,690 --> 00:05:32,650
Give me a hand pulling up these weeds.

70
00:05:32,650 --> 00:05:41,750
Now that's a harvest!

71
00:05:42,670 --> 00:05:44,970
Finally, we get to eat some normal vegetables!

72
00:05:45,590 --> 00:05:47,910
Set the weeds over here so they can dry out.

73
00:05:48,390 --> 00:05:50,070
Dead weeds make great fertilizer.

74
00:05:50,450 --> 00:05:54,390
In fact, I got a batch ready from last time that I'll bury in the golems now.

75
00:05:55,030 --> 00:05:55,290
Huh?

76
00:05:55,290 --> 00:05:58,790
These jars are filled with a different kind of fertilizer.

77
00:05:59,250 --> 00:06:02,550
I give the golem a splash of it, and it's good to go.

78
00:06:02,790 --> 00:06:03,950
I knew it!

79
00:06:04,110 --> 00:06:04,770
Knew what?

80
00:06:05,230 --> 00:06:07,490
That's how you knew where the golem's cores were.

81
00:06:07,630 --> 00:06:09,390
You plant them back each time yourself.

82
00:06:10,010 --> 00:06:11,450
It is a crime, you know.

83
00:06:11,750 --> 00:06:14,210
Tampering with magical creatures without permission.

84
00:06:14,890 --> 00:06:15,750
What crime?

85
00:06:16,050 --> 00:06:18,770
I'm just tilling soil and tending a farm.

86
00:06:19,370 --> 00:06:20,970
An illegal golem farm.

87
00:06:21,690 --> 00:06:23,830
Till the soil up good and dig some ridges.

88
00:06:23,830 --> 00:06:27,670
Also, never plant the same thing in the golem you got it from.

89
00:06:28,030 --> 00:06:30,210
Rotating crops keeps the soil working right.

90
00:06:32,990 --> 00:06:34,470
I'm so tired.

91
00:06:34,770 --> 00:06:37,450
I felt like it took more effort than fighting monsters.

92
00:06:38,110 --> 00:06:41,510
Thanks to all your help, it got done faster than if I did it myself.

93
00:06:42,470 --> 00:06:44,350
I drank so much water, I need to pee.

94
00:06:46,230 --> 00:06:47,050
All right.

95
00:06:47,370 --> 00:06:49,230
While the elf girl's in the bathroom,

96
00:06:50,130 --> 00:06:52,970
do me another favor and help me sweep up this extra dirt.

97
00:06:53,830 --> 00:07:02,670
Taro, Jiro, Saburo.

98
00:07:03,390 --> 00:07:05,770
Do they revive right away after you bury them?

99
00:07:06,310 --> 00:07:08,390
No, it takes a little while.

100
00:07:08,890 --> 00:07:10,790
The roots need time to grow enough

101
00:07:10,790 --> 00:07:14,450
so the dirt doesn't come apart when the golem gets up and moves.

102
00:07:17,450 --> 00:07:20,350
You really do care a lot about these golems.

103
00:07:21,090 --> 00:07:22,390
That's so amazing.

104
00:07:23,010 --> 00:07:24,810
And you've been doing this all by yourself.

105
00:07:25,470 --> 00:07:26,730
Hasn't that been difficult?

106
00:07:28,130 --> 00:07:29,830
Nothing hard about it at all.

107
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:31,830
It's a thing I like doing.

108
00:07:31,830 --> 00:07:36,470
We're all done.

109
00:07:36,850 --> 00:07:40,670
Now, let's have a feast of all the stuff we worked so hard to get.

110
00:07:40,670 --> 00:07:45,070
What a beautiful color.

111
00:07:46,030 --> 00:07:48,390
Guess I'm the expert at peeling things now.

112
00:07:51,090 --> 00:07:53,090
You want it smaller or is it okay?

113
00:07:53,310 --> 00:07:54,690
Nah, that's perfect.

114
00:07:56,830 --> 00:07:58,050
Need to light that fire?

115
00:07:58,270 --> 00:07:59,050
I can do it.

116
00:07:59,230 --> 00:08:01,050
I got my striker and flint for that.

117
00:08:01,590 --> 00:08:03,990
You don't have to light it that way all the time.

118
00:08:04,450 --> 00:08:05,890
It'd be faster with magic.

119
00:08:06,450 --> 00:08:09,070
How can you light golems and be anti-magic?

120
00:08:09,370 --> 00:08:11,430
Every time you do a thing the easy way,

121
00:08:11,530 --> 00:08:13,230
it dulls your skill for doing it.

122
00:08:13,690 --> 00:08:15,510
Convenient and simple ain't the same.

123
00:08:15,950 --> 00:08:17,670
Doing things your way with magic

124
00:08:17,670 --> 00:08:19,990
is the same as buying veggies at the store.

125
00:08:20,850 --> 00:08:21,250
Hmm.

126
00:08:26,850 --> 00:08:29,150
This is the last of the basilisk bacon.

127
00:08:33,990 --> 00:08:35,110
It's ready.

128
00:08:38,210 --> 00:08:39,910
Thank you for the meal.

129
00:08:42,790 --> 00:08:47,790
This is so good!

130
00:08:47,990 --> 00:08:50,650
How can something that grows underground be this delicious?

131
00:08:51,190 --> 00:08:52,990
Maybe the veggies taste so good

132
00:08:52,990 --> 00:08:54,290
because of something in the golem.

133
00:08:54,550 --> 00:08:55,050
Shut it!

134
00:08:55,350 --> 00:08:56,470
I don't care if it walks.

135
00:08:56,570 --> 00:08:57,950
It's just a veggie patch.

136
00:08:58,370 --> 00:08:59,210
By the way,

137
00:08:59,590 --> 00:09:02,310
if a golem's body is 99% dirt,

138
00:09:02,310 --> 00:09:04,550
what's the last 1% of it?

139
00:09:05,330 --> 00:09:06,210
That secret.

140
00:09:08,370 --> 00:09:08,890
Ah!

141
00:09:09,030 --> 00:09:10,410
That hit the spot.

142
00:09:11,130 --> 00:09:12,590
I'm so stuffed.

143
00:09:13,490 --> 00:09:15,510
I feel like taking a nap now.

144
00:09:16,010 --> 00:09:16,970
Go on and take one.

145
00:09:17,630 --> 00:09:20,030
I got a few chores I need to do anyway.

146
00:09:21,110 --> 00:09:21,590
Hmm.

147
00:09:22,050 --> 00:09:23,210
Help clean up.

148
00:09:23,490 --> 00:09:24,310
Gonna hit the head.

149
00:09:25,150 --> 00:09:28,350
I appreciate having a nice, clean bathroom way down here.

150
00:09:28,730 --> 00:09:31,550
It's so much better than your typical hole dug in the ground.

151
00:09:32,310 --> 00:09:34,670
In a dungeon where there's a lot of foot traffic,

152
00:09:35,030 --> 00:09:37,250
there are designated areas for restrooms.

153
00:09:38,270 --> 00:09:40,390
They're always so well-maintained.

154
00:09:40,730 --> 00:09:43,090
Some of them even have fresh flowers in them.

155
00:09:43,390 --> 00:09:45,070
I wonder who goes to all the trouble.

156
00:09:48,810 --> 00:09:49,290
Senshi!

157
00:09:49,290 --> 00:09:52,010
What is it?

158
00:09:52,010 --> 00:09:53,150
What are you doing?

159
00:09:53,790 --> 00:09:57,430
I'm gonna fill up my fertilizer pots with the slop from the toilets.

160
00:09:58,150 --> 00:10:00,450
I can't believe you can do that after eating.

161
00:10:00,790 --> 00:10:03,110
This is the best fertilizer we have down here.

162
00:10:03,530 --> 00:10:05,010
And the veggies we ate were...

163
00:10:05,750 --> 00:10:07,350
Get a grip.

164
00:10:07,810 --> 00:10:09,490
That's how it's done up top, too.

165
00:10:09,830 --> 00:10:10,850
Yeah, I know.

166
00:10:11,130 --> 00:10:12,210
It's still gross.

167
00:10:12,210 --> 00:10:13,430
Hey, Senshi.

168
00:10:13,550 --> 00:10:13,990
Hang on.

169
00:10:14,630 --> 00:10:17,030
Why do you go to all this trouble to live down here?

170
00:10:17,610 --> 00:10:20,290
No offense, but life's easier up top.

171
00:10:20,650 --> 00:10:22,070
You can still be self-sufficient

172
00:10:22,070 --> 00:10:25,290
and do all your farming and hunting and stuff like that.

173
00:10:26,370 --> 00:10:27,690
If I lived up there,

174
00:10:27,930 --> 00:10:30,530
who'd keep the bathrooms clean and stocked down here?

175
00:10:31,390 --> 00:10:34,330
When a zombie's stuck in a toilet, who'd pull it out?

176
00:10:34,890 --> 00:10:37,210
Who'd fix the golems if they fell apart?

177
00:10:37,210 --> 00:10:41,190
You know, there used to be ten walking around.

178
00:10:41,730 --> 00:10:43,290
But now, there's only three.

179
00:10:43,730 --> 00:10:46,190
If they're gone, the monsters from the lower floors

180
00:10:46,190 --> 00:10:47,810
would find their way up here.

181
00:10:48,370 --> 00:10:50,310
That'll force the monsters that live here now

182
00:10:50,310 --> 00:10:51,570
to go who knows where.

183
00:10:51,770 --> 00:10:55,210
And those monsters will force other monsters out of their homes.

184
00:10:55,790 --> 00:10:58,990
If that happens, this place will change in a bad way.

185
00:10:59,610 --> 00:11:01,770
You won't be able to hunt or even walk around.

186
00:11:02,950 --> 00:11:04,930
In dungeons, the same as a field.

187
00:11:04,930 --> 00:11:06,990
If you don't take care of it right,

188
00:11:07,290 --> 00:11:09,010
you can't enjoy what it brings you.

189
00:11:09,810 --> 00:11:13,070
My thinking is, in here, I eat what I grow or hunt.

190
00:11:13,330 --> 00:11:15,210
But I always give something back to it.

191
00:11:15,730 --> 00:11:17,950
Living like that makes me appreciate the dungeon.

192
00:11:18,450 --> 00:11:20,290
Makes me feel like when I step foot in here,

193
00:11:20,550 --> 00:11:22,050
I'm a part of it all.

194
00:11:22,890 --> 00:11:24,770
And that makes me happy.

195
00:11:26,670 --> 00:11:29,190
But if that's the case,

196
00:11:29,490 --> 00:11:32,010
is it okay to leave here to help us on our journey?

197
00:11:32,710 --> 00:11:34,570
Won't this fall apart without you?

198
00:11:35,150 --> 00:11:37,510
Nope, I don't have to be here all the time.

199
00:11:38,010 --> 00:11:40,630
The golems can take care of things for a month or two.

200
00:11:41,550 --> 00:11:44,610
Besides, if you folks up and died of malnutrition,

201
00:11:44,730 --> 00:11:45,550
I'd feel terrible.

202
00:11:46,230 --> 00:11:47,110
Wait here for me.

203
00:11:47,350 --> 00:11:48,490
I'll be done in a bit.

204
00:11:54,570 --> 00:11:56,290
Senshi is so amazing.

205
00:11:56,290 --> 00:12:02,510
What are we doing, carrying all of this?

206
00:12:02,910 --> 00:12:05,070
I use them to barter with.

207
00:12:05,210 --> 00:12:07,470
Used to sell them from a stand where I'd leave them,

208
00:12:07,590 --> 00:12:08,790
but that didn't work out.

209
00:12:09,090 --> 00:12:10,730
You just left them there?

210
00:12:10,990 --> 00:12:11,690
Honor system.

211
00:12:12,110 --> 00:12:14,290
I had a treasure chest there to drop your money,

212
00:12:14,590 --> 00:12:17,470
but the cash got stolen, so I stopped doing that.

213
00:12:17,470 --> 00:12:21,430
No wonder that treasure chest always had money in it.

214
00:12:21,930 --> 00:12:24,870
Is this floor the only one you do your bartering on?

215
00:12:25,390 --> 00:12:27,790
My usual customers are down a few floors.

216
00:12:28,170 --> 00:12:30,530
We set up a time to meet so they won't be there now.

217
00:12:30,970 --> 00:12:33,330
I didn't want to leave these rotten on the golems,

218
00:12:33,470 --> 00:12:35,150
but if we can't trade them off,

219
00:12:35,190 --> 00:12:36,210
we'll just have to toss them.

220
00:12:36,670 --> 00:12:37,210
Oh, well.

221
00:12:37,590 --> 00:12:38,830
That is out of the question.

222
00:12:38,970 --> 00:12:40,210
We can't waste this food.

223
00:12:40,630 --> 00:12:42,390
After all the work it took to grow,

224
00:12:42,930 --> 00:12:44,830
it's perfect and shiny and delicious.

225
00:12:45,190 --> 00:12:45,850
Veggie lover.

226
00:12:47,190 --> 00:12:48,330
Let's keep going.

227
00:12:48,830 --> 00:12:49,710
With any luck,

228
00:12:49,750 --> 00:12:51,870
we'll find someone on this floor who wants them.

229
00:12:53,750 --> 00:12:54,950
This'll take forever.

230
00:12:54,950 --> 00:12:57,530
Even in a dungeon,

231
00:12:57,730 --> 00:12:58,550
there are merchants.

232
00:13:03,210 --> 00:13:03,770
Enter.

233
00:13:07,670 --> 00:13:09,690
Their customers are adventurers

234
00:13:09,690 --> 00:13:11,950
and those who cannot return to the surface

235
00:13:11,950 --> 00:13:14,150
for various reasons.

236
00:13:18,190 --> 00:13:19,390
Welcome, good folk.

237
00:13:19,510 --> 00:13:19,810
Welcome.

238
00:13:20,550 --> 00:13:22,650
Will we be dining in or staying the night?

239
00:13:23,050 --> 00:13:23,990
We're here to trade.

240
00:13:23,990 --> 00:13:25,750
Ah, splendid, splendid.

241
00:13:27,210 --> 00:13:28,910
And what are we trading today?

242
00:13:29,590 --> 00:13:30,110
Vegetables.

243
00:13:32,750 --> 00:13:34,130
Get out, go on, cat!

244
00:13:34,250 --> 00:13:35,570
But, sir, just listen.

245
00:13:35,790 --> 00:13:37,850
If you want to trade something, bring gold!

246
00:13:38,110 --> 00:13:38,550
Understand?

247
00:13:39,010 --> 00:13:40,310
You do know what gold is.

248
00:13:40,610 --> 00:13:42,410
It's round and shiny and glitters!

249
00:13:43,110 --> 00:13:45,230
We don't want gems or anything valuable.

250
00:13:45,710 --> 00:13:48,090
Just some food and spices from your kitchen.

251
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:50,050
Look, isn't this round and shiny?

252
00:13:50,470 --> 00:13:52,150
Show this here carrot to your cook.

253
00:13:52,150 --> 00:13:54,470
They'll want to make something good out of it for sure.

254
00:13:54,610 --> 00:13:55,450
That's disgusting!

255
00:13:55,750 --> 00:13:57,210
Who the hell would want to eat that?

256
00:13:58,530 --> 00:14:00,270
You rotten little...

257
00:14:00,270 --> 00:14:01,890
If you treat food like that,

258
00:14:01,950 --> 00:14:03,750
I swear you'll get yours in the end!

259
00:14:03,750 --> 00:14:06,430
What are you waiting for?

260
00:14:06,430 --> 00:14:08,190
Throw these idiots out of here already!

261
00:14:08,230 --> 00:14:09,010
Just listen!

262
00:14:17,690 --> 00:14:18,170
Orcs!

263
00:14:18,590 --> 00:14:20,790
First ones to die are the ones with the weapons!

264
00:14:21,190 --> 00:14:21,430
Go!

265
00:14:21,570 --> 00:14:21,970
Kill them!

266
00:14:22,130 --> 00:14:23,310
Kill every one of them!

267
00:14:23,310 --> 00:14:30,090
Why are orcs here?

268
00:14:30,410 --> 00:14:32,450
They're supposed to live on the lower floors!

269
00:14:32,750 --> 00:14:33,990
Who cares about that?

270
00:14:34,090 --> 00:14:35,310
We have to...

271
00:14:35,310 --> 00:14:40,050
Marcel!

272
00:14:40,050 --> 00:14:50,270
What do you think you're doing hanging around a dump like this, Senshi?

273
00:14:51,730 --> 00:14:53,910
I was gonna ask you the same thing.

274
00:14:56,290 --> 00:14:58,510
You in a party with this lot?

275
00:14:58,990 --> 00:14:59,790
That's right.

276
00:15:00,790 --> 00:15:02,150
Humans and elves.

277
00:15:02,150 --> 00:15:05,650
Don't tell me your usual customers.

278
00:15:06,290 --> 00:15:06,770
Yep.

279
00:15:06,950 --> 00:15:07,430
It's them.

280
00:15:09,430 --> 00:15:12,110
I had a feeling he did business with a rough crowd.

281
00:15:12,330 --> 00:15:12,930
But orcs?

282
00:15:13,170 --> 00:15:14,790
I thought they'd be goblins.

283
00:15:15,150 --> 00:15:15,570
Really?

284
00:15:15,730 --> 00:15:17,090
I was sure they'd be kobolds.

285
00:15:17,610 --> 00:15:19,690
I seen the red dragon.

286
00:15:20,970 --> 00:15:23,710
The damn thing used to keep to itself.

287
00:15:24,390 --> 00:15:25,130
Not anymore.

288
00:15:25,770 --> 00:15:27,370
He's been showing up near our village,

289
00:15:27,650 --> 00:15:30,090
sniffing around and blowing fire all over.

290
00:15:30,090 --> 00:15:33,470
We gots kids and old orcs to take cares of.

291
00:15:33,910 --> 00:15:34,830
They can't fight,

292
00:15:35,070 --> 00:15:37,350
so we came up to this floor till the dragon left.

293
00:15:37,950 --> 00:15:39,490
You think that could be our dragon?

294
00:15:39,790 --> 00:15:40,290
Tell me.

295
00:15:40,710 --> 00:15:41,610
Where did you see it?

296
00:15:42,210 --> 00:15:43,450
You think I'd tell you,

297
00:15:43,610 --> 00:15:45,490
a human, where our village is?

298
00:15:46,050 --> 00:15:47,070
Fat chance.

299
00:15:47,630 --> 00:15:49,670
Chief, we done killing everyone.

300
00:15:50,190 --> 00:15:50,990
Ah, great.

301
00:15:51,190 --> 00:15:53,230
Pack up whatever's not nailed down, then.

302
00:15:53,650 --> 00:15:55,050
What is this, milk?

303
00:15:56,610 --> 00:15:57,570
It's rotten.

304
00:15:58,130 --> 00:15:58,810
Chuck it.

305
00:15:58,810 --> 00:16:01,930
Them veggies be something you grew, I guess.

306
00:16:02,510 --> 00:16:04,950
We're on a supply run looking for food.

307
00:16:05,610 --> 00:16:07,550
Appreciate if you'd share that with us.

308
00:16:07,790 --> 00:16:08,910
Sure, be happy to.

309
00:16:09,550 --> 00:16:10,910
What you got to trade for it?

310
00:16:11,170 --> 00:16:11,930
No trade.

311
00:16:12,390 --> 00:16:13,250
Tribe's desperate.

312
00:16:14,110 --> 00:16:16,370
We barely got up to this floor alive.

313
00:16:16,370 --> 00:16:20,050
You've been a good friend and I hate to do this,

314
00:16:20,150 --> 00:16:23,750
but hand over everything you got right now.

315
00:16:26,190 --> 00:16:27,590
Can't you reason with him?

316
00:16:28,590 --> 00:16:29,290
All right.

317
00:16:29,690 --> 00:16:30,870
Glad to hear that.

318
00:16:31,370 --> 00:16:33,870
I want to ask you for a favor in return, though.

319
00:16:34,670 --> 00:16:37,330
Let me and my party spend a night with your tribe.

320
00:16:37,330 --> 00:16:38,210
What?

321
00:16:39,010 --> 00:16:41,230
Do me that favor and you can have my veggies,

322
00:16:41,450 --> 00:16:43,450
my life, hell, anything you want.

323
00:16:43,790 --> 00:16:44,150
Huh?

324
00:16:44,630 --> 00:16:45,530
Also, you there.

325
00:16:45,650 --> 00:16:45,990
Me?

326
00:16:46,270 --> 00:16:48,150
That stuff's not rotten, it's fermented.

327
00:16:48,450 --> 00:16:49,710
Don't you dare throw it away.

328
00:16:49,850 --> 00:16:50,250
Bring it.

329
00:16:50,250 --> 00:16:56,090
They took all our weapons away.

330
00:16:56,190 --> 00:16:57,750
How could you put us in this position?

331
00:16:58,150 --> 00:17:00,370
If we find out where they set their camp up,

332
00:17:00,550 --> 00:17:02,370
we'll never see the surface again.

333
00:17:02,770 --> 00:17:04,010
Tell me you have a plan.

334
00:17:04,130 --> 00:17:05,150
Please tell me you got a plan.

335
00:17:05,530 --> 00:17:06,150
Mm-hmm.

336
00:17:06,750 --> 00:17:09,970
That jar I told the orc not to throw out's got yeast in it.

337
00:17:10,190 --> 00:17:11,630
Yeast is a leavening agent.

338
00:17:12,090 --> 00:17:13,930
And I don't know if you noticed,

339
00:17:13,930 --> 00:17:17,610
but the orcs also grabbed every sack of flour in the kitchen.

340
00:17:17,970 --> 00:17:19,550
You know what that means, don't you?

341
00:17:19,550 --> 00:17:20,970
Uh, no.

342
00:17:22,050 --> 00:17:23,790
We can make bread!

343
00:17:24,470 --> 00:17:24,990
Dummy!

344
00:17:25,290 --> 00:17:26,430
Wait, so you don't have bread!

345
00:17:26,430 --> 00:17:27,550
I don't know how stupid you are!

346
00:17:27,550 --> 00:17:28,950
You don't have bread!

347
00:17:29,430 --> 00:17:30,250
Not one bread!

348
00:17:30,510 --> 00:17:31,730
Fight down, you savages!

349
00:17:35,330 --> 00:17:36,570
Is that an elf?

350
00:17:36,830 --> 00:17:38,370
What a barbaric face.

351
00:17:39,230 --> 00:17:40,850
You have to stay in this pen.

352
00:17:41,530 --> 00:17:42,810
Dad's back from pillaging.

353
00:17:43,570 --> 00:17:47,210
We won't end up as ingredients in their dinner, will we?

354
00:17:47,210 --> 00:17:49,970
What did you do with that jar of leavening agent?

355
00:17:50,270 --> 00:17:50,530
Huh?

356
00:17:50,810 --> 00:17:53,310
You don't know what it is, you don't know how to use it,

357
00:17:53,330 --> 00:17:54,170
so give it to me!

358
00:17:54,510 --> 00:17:55,190
Come on!

359
00:17:55,430 --> 00:17:56,990
I can make bread with it!

360
00:17:57,450 --> 00:17:57,750
Bread!

361
00:17:58,010 --> 00:17:58,270
Bread!

362
00:17:58,530 --> 00:17:58,790
Bread!

363
00:17:59,030 --> 00:17:59,310
Bread!

364
00:17:59,550 --> 00:17:59,730
Bread!

365
00:17:59,730 --> 00:17:59,790
Bread!

366
00:17:59,790 --> 00:18:05,730
Put flour, salt, sugar, leavening agent, and water in a bowl.

367
00:18:06,010 --> 00:18:06,870
Then knead it.

368
00:18:07,410 --> 00:18:09,290
Work that sucker till it's nice and firm.

369
00:18:10,450 --> 00:18:12,050
Are you playing with mud?

370
00:18:12,170 --> 00:18:13,130
Uh, huh?

371
00:18:13,130 --> 00:18:16,650
Time for your history lesson, kiddo.

372
00:18:16,650 --> 00:18:22,430
In the old days, we lived up top, not here in the underground, like the bugs.

373
00:18:23,410 --> 00:18:29,090
Humans and elves like those ones murdered most of our kin and stole the land we had up there.

374
00:18:29,910 --> 00:18:33,270
I seem to remember orcs did a whole lot of murdering, too.

375
00:18:33,510 --> 00:18:34,030
Was that?

376
00:18:34,310 --> 00:18:36,350
Now's a good time to add the olive oil.

377
00:18:36,350 --> 00:18:43,510
Anyway, they chased us down to the underground, and our tribe found a new home.

378
00:18:43,830 --> 00:18:48,350
For a long time, we lived in peace, till their kind found us again.

379
00:18:48,790 --> 00:18:52,930
To knead, you hold the edge, then smack it down again and again.

380
00:18:53,270 --> 00:18:56,450
They poured oil in our caves and set fire to it.

381
00:18:56,690 --> 00:19:01,890
That's because your people wouldn't stop raiding the villages of every other race in the land.

382
00:19:02,390 --> 00:19:04,630
We was doing what we had to to survive.

383
00:19:04,630 --> 00:19:07,950
All orcs ever did was rob and kill and terrorize everyone.

384
00:19:08,170 --> 00:19:09,590
That's why you were chased here.

385
00:19:09,910 --> 00:19:11,670
Come on, Marsau, stop it.

386
00:19:11,870 --> 00:19:12,650
We're their guests.

387
00:19:12,770 --> 00:19:13,530
Shut your hole!

388
00:19:13,650 --> 00:19:16,510
Get your fingers in there and work that dough!

389
00:19:16,770 --> 00:19:17,170
Sorry.

390
00:19:18,050 --> 00:19:18,910
Give me that.

391
00:19:19,130 --> 00:19:19,850
I'll do it.

392
00:19:20,550 --> 00:19:22,290
Your kind chased my tribe underground.

393
00:19:22,810 --> 00:19:26,130
We found this dungeon and made it our home, and you come here to steal it.

394
00:19:26,890 --> 00:19:30,110
It was the villagers who were the first to discover this dungeon.

395
00:19:30,490 --> 00:19:33,310
But us orcs were the first to come down this deep.

396
00:19:33,310 --> 00:19:36,250
If that's where you want to go with it, then zombies were here first!

397
00:19:36,290 --> 00:19:39,450
Once you get it stretching easy, it's time for the first proofing.

398
00:19:39,450 --> 00:19:45,670
When the dough gets twice as big, cut it into equal pieces.

399
00:19:45,910 --> 00:19:47,230
Then shape with your hands.

400
00:19:48,770 --> 00:19:50,770
Why you been so quiet, Tallman?

401
00:19:50,870 --> 00:19:51,030
Huh?

402
00:19:51,090 --> 00:19:53,130
Don't you have no opinion on things?

403
00:19:53,670 --> 00:20:00,070
Rumors say if a body defeats the mad mage that built this dungeon, a body gets to rule the castle.

404
00:20:00,770 --> 00:20:03,670
You must be here to get to the bottom of this dungeon.

405
00:20:03,670 --> 00:20:08,470
When you get your kingdom, what you gonna do then?

406
00:20:08,470 --> 00:20:14,450
I know all about that rumor, too, but I never thought about it that much.

407
00:20:15,310 --> 00:20:16,470
Typical adventurer.

408
00:20:17,250 --> 00:20:19,530
If I cut down to the bone, you're all the same.

409
00:20:20,170 --> 00:20:21,630
A bunch of greedy idiots.

410
00:20:22,290 --> 00:20:24,470
All you care about is gold and power.

411
00:20:25,030 --> 00:20:30,190
The thought someone like that could rule this place makes my hair stand up all prickly-like.

412
00:20:30,190 --> 00:20:34,710
That's how come if we see a surface dweller down here, we'd kill him.

413
00:20:34,890 --> 00:20:35,970
Okay, that does it!

414
00:20:36,350 --> 00:20:38,790
If you're so noble, take over the castle yourself!

415
00:20:38,910 --> 00:20:41,650
Or is stealing stuff the only thing orcs are good at doing?

416
00:20:42,350 --> 00:20:44,150
You got guts, elf girl.

417
00:20:44,890 --> 00:20:45,750
I like you.

418
00:20:45,990 --> 00:20:48,030
I'm gonna throw you in the fire myself!

419
00:20:48,430 --> 00:20:50,910
See? The only thing you know how to do is violence!

420
00:20:51,450 --> 00:20:52,510
Let it prove some more.

421
00:20:52,510 --> 00:21:00,990
Then, once it finishes rising, set it down over some low heat.

422
00:21:01,730 --> 00:21:09,470
Steam it for a little bit, and when you open the lid, we got ourselves some bread!

423
00:21:10,250 --> 00:21:11,570
It smells amazing!

424
00:21:12,070 --> 00:21:13,370
Let's have a taste.

425
00:21:13,790 --> 00:21:18,610
Hold it! That bread belongs to my tribe, and we're not giving you any.

426
00:21:18,990 --> 00:21:19,370
What?

427
00:21:19,370 --> 00:21:23,030
You said you wanted to make bread, and we let you make it.

428
00:21:23,370 --> 00:21:25,390
But we decide what to do with it.

429
00:21:27,830 --> 00:21:28,310
Daddy?

430
00:21:28,730 --> 00:21:29,030
Hmm?

431
00:21:29,790 --> 00:21:31,030
We all made it together.

432
00:21:31,410 --> 00:21:33,490
Why can't we all eat it together, too?

433
00:21:37,250 --> 00:21:40,010
It's not a proper meal if you only have bread.

434
00:21:40,810 --> 00:21:43,250
Main dish, side dish, and veggies.

435
00:21:43,590 --> 00:21:45,690
You need all of those for a balanced meal.

436
00:21:45,690 --> 00:21:49,850
Your daddy there? He just wanted to wait until all the other dishes were ready.

437
00:21:50,310 --> 00:21:51,530
Hold your tongue, elf!

438
00:21:52,050 --> 00:21:52,770
She's right.

439
00:21:53,170 --> 00:21:56,710
Your pop said we could stay with your family if we let him have our vegetables.

440
00:21:57,470 --> 00:22:00,430
And your daddy's an orc who always keeps his word.

441
00:22:05,190 --> 00:22:05,670
Hey!

442
00:22:06,170 --> 00:22:07,770
Get them whatever they need.

443
00:22:07,770 --> 00:22:17,630
There. It's ready.

444
00:22:19,070 --> 00:22:19,850
Eat up!

445
00:22:20,030 --> 00:22:21,030
It looks yummy.

446
00:22:21,030 --> 00:22:30,190
Whoa, it's good!

447
00:22:32,590 --> 00:22:33,910
It's good and spicy!

448
00:22:34,690 --> 00:22:39,810
We used the same ingredients as we did for your stewed cabbage, but this tastes totally different.

449
00:22:40,810 --> 00:22:43,110
Before, I said orcs are only good at stealing.

450
00:22:43,550 --> 00:22:45,270
But you're pretty good cooks, too.

451
00:22:45,270 --> 00:22:47,070
Shudderholm.

452
00:22:48,350 --> 00:22:52,930
Um, earlier you asked why I wanted to get to the bottom of the dungeon.

453
00:22:53,810 --> 00:22:56,010
My sister was eaten by a red dragon.

454
00:22:56,550 --> 00:22:58,450
And we're just trying to find it.

455
00:22:59,450 --> 00:23:03,710
But if you can tell us where you saw it, we can go find it and kill it.

456
00:23:04,210 --> 00:23:07,110
We won't go near your village or tell anyone about it.

457
00:23:07,110 --> 00:23:13,330
I swear.

458
00:23:18,550 --> 00:23:19,110
Hey!

459
00:23:19,570 --> 00:23:20,730
Get me that map!

460
00:23:20,890 --> 00:23:21,350
On it!

461
00:23:22,430 --> 00:23:27,430
We saw it two floors down from here, near the living quarters on the west side.

462
00:23:28,230 --> 00:23:29,230
Thanks a lot.

463
00:23:32,230 --> 00:23:32,790
Hmm.

464
00:23:32,790 --> 00:23:39,750
From now on, I promise I'll think hard about what to do if I end up ruling the castle.

465
00:23:40,370 --> 00:23:40,770
Ha!

466
00:23:41,210 --> 00:23:46,010
To think a guy caught by orcs and forced to make bread could ever be a king of anything.

467
00:23:47,290 --> 00:23:49,110
Well, good luck to you.

468
00:23:51,110 --> 00:23:52,910
Thanks, that's funny.

469
00:23:54,510 --> 00:23:54,910
Ow!

470
00:23:56,450 --> 00:23:59,910
Did you know that cabbage was grown on the back of a golem?

471
00:23:59,910 --> 00:24:07,930
Opinions may differ, but we can all agree, we get hungry.

472
00:24:10,390 --> 00:24:12,870
Delicious dungeon food brings folks together.

473
00:24:13,290 --> 00:24:14,810
Delicious in dungeon.

